{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#841","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#841","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#841\",\"parent_revision\":\"58f4b359ee0bb764120bd20cb274708cbe161bf1\",\"root_revision\":\"d23393e4bc5c040caf06149ecf2766a43203f7edd081e8ddd7b8d92c1579239b\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe code-reviewer agent produces follow-up task files that do not conform to SAM filename conventions (expected: plan/tasks-{N}-{slug}-followup-{k}.md) or use the correct task key format. This causes downstream routing failures in /complete-implementation when it attempts to detect and process follow-up files by name pattern, and when backlog-linking logic derives search titles from filenames. Success looks like: code-reviewer follow-up files use the exact SAM filename pattern, task keys within those files match the format expected by sam CLI and task_status_hook.py, and /complete-implementation can detect, route, and attach them to backlog items without manual intervention.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **fix code-reviewer agent to produce sam-format follow-up task files with correct filename convention and task key format** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Agent task \u2014 auto-derived from title\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-18\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-02)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n7/10 \u2014 Follow-up task files that don't match the SAM filename pattern are silently orphaned: `/complete-implementation` glob fails to find them, backlog-linking never runs, and recursion gate never fires. Any code review that surfaces actionable work loses that work.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: All downstream routing in `/complete-implementation` Phase 1 post-dispatch (Step 1 of Recursive Follow-up Handling)\\n- Bottleneck: Code reviewer findings become dead artifacts \u2014 not linked to backlog, not routed for implementation\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Follow-up task files produced by code-reviewer are automatically detected by `/complete-implementation` via the `P*-{slug}-followup-*.yaml` glob\\n- Backlog-linking derives the correct search slug from the filename, enabling match-or-create routing\\n- Recursion gate can evaluate same-scope / high-priority follow-ups for immediate execution\\n- Task keys recognized by `sam_schema` and `task_status_hook.py` (which parses task IDs from plan files)\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen `code-reviewer` finds issues during a quality gate run, it creates follow-up plan files via `mcp__plugin_dh_sam__sam_create`. The created files are stored at `~/.dh/projects/{project-slug}/plan/P{NNN}-{feature-slug}-followup-{k}.yaml`. The `tasks:` YAML block within each file uses `task:` as the identifier field (e.g. `task: T1`). After Phase 1 completes, `/complete-implementation` globs `P*-{slug}-followup-*.yaml`, finds the files, derives search slugs, and routes each file to a backlog item.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nBoth `plugins/python3-development/agents/code-reviewer.md` and `plugins/python-engineering/agents/code-reviewer.md` instruct the agent to:\\n1. Call `mcp__plugin_dh_sam__sam_create` with `slug=\\\"{feature-slug}-followup-{k}\\\"` \u2014 producing a `P{NNN}-{feature-slug}-followup-{k}.yaml` file in the DH plan directory\\n2. Use `task:` (not `id:`) as the task identifier key in the `tasks_yaml` argument\\n3. Report the created file path in the ARTIFACTS `Task files:` list\\n\\nThe `python-engineering` code-reviewer currently has no follow-up task creation instructions at all; it needs the same `## Task File Format` section that `python3-development` has (lines 167\u2013247).\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. Running `mcp__plugin_dh_sam__sam_create(slug=\\\"{feature-slug}-followup-1\\\", ...)` produces a file matching `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/plan/P{NNN}-{feature-slug}-followup-1.yaml`\\n2. The `tasks_yaml` passed by code-reviewer uses `task: T1` (not `id: T1`) \u2014 verifiable by reading the created YAML file\\n3. After a code-reviewer run, the glob `~/.dh/projects/{project-slug}/plan/P*-{slug}-followup-*.yaml` returns at least one result matching the produced file\\n4. `/complete-implementation` Step 1 (Detect Follow-up Files) finds the file without falling back to ARTIFACTS parsing alone\\n5. The slug-derivation algorithm (strip `P{NNN}-` prefix, strip `-followup-{k}.yaml` suffix, replace hyphens with spaces) produces a string that matches a backlog item title or topic \u2014 verifiable via `backlog_list(title=\\\"{derived-slug}\\\")`\\n6. `python-engineering:code-reviewer` produces follow-up files using the same MCP-based approach as `python3-development:code-reviewer`\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Agent | plugins/python3-development/agents/code-reviewer.md (lines 167\u2013247: Task File Format section \u2014 the reference implementation) |\\n| Agent | plugins/python-engineering/agents/code-reviewer.md (lines 1\u201364: current state \u2014 no follow-up file creation instructions) |\\n| Skill | plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md (lines 524\u2013605: Recursive Follow-up Handling, including the glob pattern and slug-derivation algorithm) |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py (task ID regex `_TASK_ID_RE` at line 73 \u2014 must match format used in follow-up files) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None\\n- Blocks: Recursive follow-up routing in `/complete-implementation`; backlog item auto-linking for code-review findings\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 the `python3-development` code-reviewer already has the correct instructions (lines 167\u2013247). The fix is: (1) verify `python3-development` code-reviewer `slug` argument format matches the glob pattern exactly, (2) copy/adapt the `## Task File Format` section into `python-engineering` code-reviewer, (3) confirm both agents report file paths in ARTIFACTS `Task files:` list. No schema changes needed.\\n\",\"digest\":\"2396ad3b685befac445b2029154b4382f4072e62d01985049f8b6b3e84b4553f\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPgyrAg\"}"}